what does a typical day of a consultant  at mckinsey bcg or bane look like caveat  of course every project is different but  this should give you a good idea at 8 30  in the morning you might meet with your  team in the team room to go over a  check-in together with the project lead  everyone will discuss his or her  priorities for the day at 9 00 am you  might have a meeting with a client from  the finance team to go over some numbers  that the person sent to you and ask some  terrifying questions on the data you  received at 10 you might sit together  with a line manager from the client to  get additional input for your analysis  then you might have two hours for  yourself in the team room to get some  work done at midday you go to the  canteen of your client together with  some colleagues to grab some lunch  afterwards one of your partners one of  the senior leaders of your firm might  fly in and meet you for one or two hours  of problem-solving session then around 6  pm you might do a team checkout where  everyone shares the progress of the day  and also discusses what they still have  on their plate for the remainder of the  evening around 7pm you might drive to  the hotel 14 dinner when everyone goes  to the hotel room to wrap up the day if  you would be able to close your laptop  at 10 pm that wouldn't be too bad follow  for more korean sites
 

